{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019asPD5jjgtkdPo6CXLUw5u","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-b8r — Acceptance Criteria: M1 Strategy 3 — 52-Week High Momentum / Breakout\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-b8r  \n4\t**Parent:** QuantAgent-l0h (AC3)  \n5\t**Type:** Acceptance Tests  \n6\t**Created:** 2026-05-05  \n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## AC1 — Strategy class exists and satisfies the `TradingStrategy` ABC\n11\t\n12\t**Given** `quantagent/strategy/fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py` is present in the repo  \n13\t**When** `from quantagent.strategy.fifty_two_week_high_strategy import FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy` is executed  \n14\t**Then**:\n15\t- No import errors\n16\t- `issubclass(FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy, TradingStrategy)` is `True`\n17\t- Instantiation with default parameters succeeds: `FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy()`\n18\t- `FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy` appears in `quantagent/strategy/__init__.py` exports\n19\t\n20\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_class_is_valid_strategy`\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## AC2 — 52-week high calculation is correct\n25\t\n26\t### AC2.1 — Rolling max over lookback window\n27\t\n28\t**Given** a DataFrame where the `high` column has a known maximum value at position `-(lookback_days+1)` to `-1` (excluding current bar)  \n29\t**When** `_compute_52w_high()` is called  \n30\t**Then** the returned value equals the known maximum\n31\t\n32\t### AC2.2 — Current bar excluded from lookback\n33\t\n34\t**Given** a kline series where the current (last) candle has an artificially high `high` value  \n35\t**When** `_compute_52w_high()` is called  \n36\t**Then** the current candle's high is NOT included in the 52w high calculation\n37\t\n38\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"52w_high\"`\n39\t\n40\t---\n41\t\n42\t## AC3 — Trend filter activates correctly\n43\t\n44\t### AC3.1 — Price above SMA → trend filter passes\n45\t\n46\t**Given** a kline series where the closing prices trend upward and `current_price > SMA(close, 50)[-1]`  \n47\t**When** `generate_signal()` evaluates the trend condition  \n48\t**Then** the trend filter does not block a breakout signal\n49\t\n50\t### AC3.2 — Price below SMA → trend filter blocks signal\n51\t\n52\t**Given** a kline series where `current_price < SMA(close, 50)[-1]` even though price breaks the 52w high  \n53\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n54\t**Then** return value is `None`\n55\t\n56\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"trend_filter\"`\n57\t\n58\t---\n59\t\n60\t## AC4 — Volume filter activates correctly\n61\t\n62\t### AC4.1 — Volume above threshold → volume filter passes\n63\t\n64\t**Given** a kline series where the last candle's volume is `> volume_factor × volume_MA`  \n65\t**When** `generate_signal()` evaluates the volume condition  \n66\t**Then** the volume filter does not block a breakout signal\n67\t\n68\t### AC4.2 — Low volume breakout → volume filter blocks signal\n69\t\n70\t**Given** a kline series where price breaks above 52w high but last candle volume is `< volume_factor × volume_MA`  \n71\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n72\t**Then** return value is `None`\n73\t\n74\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"volume_filter\"`\n75\t\n76\t---\n77\t\n78\t## AC5 — Breakout condition\n79\t\n80\t### AC5.1 — No breakout → no signal\n81\t\n82\t**Given** `current_price <= high_52w` (even if ratio is close, e.g., 0.99)  \n83\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called with trend and volume filters passing  \n84\t**Then** return value is `None`\n85\t\n86\t### AC5.2 — Exact equality → no signal\n87\t\n88\t**Given** `current_price == high_52w`  \n89\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n90\t**Then** return value is `None` (strict `>` comparison required)\n91\t\n92\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"breakout\"`\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## AC6 — Combined: `generate_signal` produces correct LONG decision\n97\t\n98\t### AC6.1 — All conditions pass → LONG signal\n99\t\n100\t**Given** deterministic kline_data (≥ 303 candles) where:\n101\t- `current_price > high_52w` (breakout)\n102\t- `current_price > SMA(close, 50)[-1]` (uptrend)\n103\t- `volume[-1] > 1.5 × vol_MA[-1]` (volume confirmation)\n104\t\n105\t**When** `strategy.generate_signal(kline_data, \"AAPL\", \"1d\", current_price)` is called  \n106\t**Then**:\n107\t- Return value is a `TradingSignal` (not `None`)\n108\t- `signal.decision == \"LONG\"`\n109\t- `signal.confidence` is in `[0.1, 1.0]`\n110\t- `signal.entry_price == current_price`\n111\t- `signal.stop_loss == current_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n112\t- `signal.take_profit == current_price * (1 + take_profit_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n113\t- `signal.reasoning` contains \"52w-high\" (breakout is named in the reasoning string)\n114\t- `signal.exit_policy == ExitPolicy.TRAILING_STOP`\n115\t\n116\t### AC6.2 — No SHORT signals ever produced\n117\t\n118\t**Given** any kline_data and any `current_price`  \n119\t**When** `generate_signal()` returns a non-`None` value  \n120\t**Then** `signal.decision != \"SHORT\"` always\n121\t\n122\t### AC6.3 — Trend filter fails alone → `None`\n123\t\n124\t**Given** breakout and volume conditions pass but `current_price < SMA[-1]`  \n125\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n126\t**Then** return value is `None`\n127\t\n128\t### AC6.4 — Volume filter fails alone → `None`\n129\t\n130\t**Given** breakout and trend conditions pass but volume is insufficient  \n131\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n132\t**Then** return value is `None`\n133\t\n134\t### AC6.5 — Fewer than min candles → `None` without exception\n135\t\n136\t**Given** `len(kline_data) < lookback_days + max(trend_ma_period, volume_ma_period) + 1`  \n137\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n138\t**Then** return value is `None` and no exception is raised\n139\t\n140\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"generate_signal\"`\n141\t\n142\t---\n143\t\n144\t## AC7 — Confidence calculation\n145\t\n146\t**Given** a breakout where `current_price` is 5% above `high_52w`  \n147\t**When** `generate_signal()` returns a signal  \n148\t**Then** `signal.confidence` equals `max(0.1, min(1.0, 0.05 * 10))` = `0.5` (within float tolerance)\n149\t\n150\t**Given** a breakout where `current_price` is 0.5% above `high_52w`  \n151\t**When** `generate_signal()` returns a signal  \n152\t**Then** `signal.confidence == 0.1` (floor applied)\n153\t\n154\t**Given** a breakout where `current_price` is 15% above `high_52w`  \n155\t**When** `generate_signal()` returns a signal  \n156\t**Then** `signal.confidence == 1.0` (cap applied)\n157\t\n158\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"confidence\"`\n159\t\n160\t---\n161\t\n162\t## AC8 — Non-HOLD signal generated in realistic scenario\n163\t\n164\t**Given** a synthetic 400-candle daily dataset designed with:\n165\t- A clear 6-month trend upward (SMA upward)\n166\t- Normal volume for most bars, with a spike on the last bar\n167\t- The last candle's close price slightly above the rolling 252-bar high\n168\t\n169\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called on the last candle  \n170\t**Then** the return value is a `TradingSignal` with `decision == \"LONG\"`, proving the strategy is not permanently stuck in HOLD\n171\t\n172\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_generates_signal_in_realistic_scenario`\n173\t\n174\t---\n175\t\n176\t## AC9 — `should_reevaluate` always returns False\n177\t\n178\t**Given** any `ActivePosition` and `current_price`  \n179\t**When** `strategy.should_reevaluate(position, current_price)` is called  \n180\t**Then** the return value is `False`\n181\t\n182\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_should_reevaluate_false`\n183\t\n184\t---\n185\t\n186\t## AC10 — Reference backtest completes without crash and PnL is calculated\n187\t\n188\t**Given** a test environment with database configured and AAPL daily data available for 2022–2023\n189\t\n190\t**When** the reference backtest from `QuantAgent-b8r-IM` is run:\n191\t```python\n192\tstrategy = FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy()\n193\tbacktest = Backtest(\n194\t    start_date=datetime(2022, 1, 1),\n195\t    end_date=datetime(2023, 12, 31),\n196\t    assets=[\"AAPL\"],\n197\t    timeframe=\"1d\",\n198\t    initial_capital=100_000.0,\n199\t    strategy=strategy,\n200\t)\n201\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"QuantAgent-b8r-reference\")\n202\t```\n203\t\n204\t**Then**:\n205\t- `backtest.run()` completes without raising any exception\n206\t- `metrics.total_pnl` is a finite float (positive, negative, or zero)\n207\t- `metrics.total_trades >= 0`\n208\t- The run is logged with a name containing \"QuantAgent-b8r\"\n209\t\n210\t**Testable:** Manual integration test or `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_backtest_integration -m integration`\n211\t\n212\t---\n213\t\n214\t## Non-goals (explicitly excluded)\n215\t\n216\t- Performance targets (win rate, Sharpe ratio, drawdown)\n217\t- Short-selling signals or short-side momentum\n218\t- Proximity signal (without full breakout)\n219\t- Multi-symbol parallel validation\n220\t- Provider-specific behaviour or LLM integration\n221\t- Comparison against RSI, Triple Screen, or LLMAgentStrategy\n222\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7c02214-d66b-4564-be8f-476a12f21292","uuid":"3b91a6aa-b3c7-42ba-98ce-3487a47c964a","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:46:55.255Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/autodev-worktrees/techlead-20260505T213844Z/QuantAgent-b8r/implementer-20260505T213930Z/docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-b8r-AC-52week-high-momentum.md","content":"# QuantAgent-b8r — Acceptance Criteria: M1 Strategy 3 — 52-Week High Momentum / Breakout\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-b8r  \n**Parent:** QuantAgent-l0h (AC3)  \n**Type:** Acceptance Tests  \n**Created:** 2026-05-05  \n\n---\n\n## AC1 — Strategy class exists and satisfies the `TradingStrategy` ABC\n\n**Given** `quantagent/strategy/fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py` is present in the repo  \n**When** `from quantagent.strategy.fifty_two_week_high_strategy import FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy` is executed  \n**Then**:\n- No import errors\n- `issubclass(FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy, TradingStrategy)` is `True`\n- Instantiation with default parameters succeeds: `FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy()`\n- `FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy` appears in `quantagent/strategy/__init__.py` exports\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_class_is_valid_strategy`\n\n---\n\n## AC2 — 52-week high calculation is correct\n\n### AC2.1 — Rolling max over lookback window\n\n**Given** a DataFrame where the `high` column has a known maximum value at position `-(lookback_days+1)` to `-1` (excluding current bar)  \n**When** `_compute_52w_high()` is called  \n**Then** the returned value equals the known maximum\n\n### AC2.2 — Current bar excluded from lookback\n\n**Given** a kline series where the current (last) candle has an artificially high `high` value  \n**When** `_compute_52w_high()` is called  \n**Then** the current candle's high is NOT included in the 52w high calculation\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"52w_high\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC3 — Trend filter activates correctly\n\n### AC3.1 — Price above SMA → trend filter passes\n\n**Given** a kline series where the closing prices trend upward and `current_price > SMA(close, 50)[-1]`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` evaluates the trend condition  \n**Then** the trend filter does not block a breakout signal\n\n### AC3.2 — Price below SMA → trend filter blocks signal\n\n**Given** a kline series where `current_price < SMA(close, 50)[-1]` even though price breaks the 52w high  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"trend_filter\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC4 — Volume filter activates correctly\n\n### AC4.1 — Volume above threshold → volume filter passes\n\n**Given** a kline series where the last candle's volume is `> volume_factor × volume_MA`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` evaluates the volume condition  \n**Then** the volume filter does not block a breakout signal\n\n### AC4.2 — Low volume breakout → volume filter blocks signal\n\n**Given** a kline series where price breaks above 52w high but last candle volume is `< volume_factor × volume_MA`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"volume_filter\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC5 — Breakout condition\n\n### AC5.1 — No breakout → no signal\n\n**Given** `current_price <= high_52w` (even if ratio is close, e.g., 0.99)  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called with trend and volume filters passing  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n### AC5.2 — Exact equality → no signal\n\n**Given** `current_price == high_52w`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None` (strict `>` comparison required)\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"breakout\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC6 — Combined: `generate_signal` produces correct LONG decision\n\n### AC6.1 — All conditions pass → LONG signal\n\n**Given** deterministic kline_data (≥ 303 candles) where:\n- `current_price > high_52w` (breakout)\n- `current_price > SMA(close, 50)[-1]` (uptrend)\n- `volume[-1] > 1.5 × vol_MA[-1]` (volume confirmation)\n\n**When** `strategy.generate_signal(kline_data, \"AAPL\", \"1d\", current_price)` is called  \n**Then**:\n- Return value is a `TradingSignal` (not `None`)\n- `signal.decision == \"LONG\"`\n- `signal.confidence` is in `[0.1, 1.0]`\n- `signal.entry_price == current_price`\n- `signal.stop_loss == current_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n- `signal.take_profit == current_price * (1 + take_profit_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n- `signal.reasoning` contains \"52w-high\" (breakout is named in the reasoning string)\n- `signal.exit_policy == ExitPolicy.TRAILING_STOP`\n\n### AC6.2 — No SHORT signals ever produced\n\n**Given** any kline_data and any `current_price`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` returns a non-`None` value  \n**Then** `signal.decision != \"SHORT\"` always\n\n### AC6.3 — Trend filter fails alone → `None`\n\n**Given** breakout and volume conditions pass but `current_price < SMA[-1]`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n### AC6.4 — Volume filter fails alone → `None`\n\n**Given** breakout and trend conditions pass but volume is insufficient  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n### AC6.5 — Fewer than min candles → `None` without exception\n\n**Given** `len(kline_data) < lookback_days + max(trend_ma_period, volume_ma_period) + 1`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None` and no exception is raised\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"generate_signal\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC7 — Confidence calculation\n\n**Given** a breakout where `current_price` is 5% above `high_52w`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` returns a signal  \n**Then** `signal.confidence` equals `max(0.1, min(1.0, 0.05 * 10))` = `0.5` (within float tolerance)\n\n**Given** a breakout where `current_price` is 0.5% above `high_52w`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` returns a signal  \n**Then** `signal.confidence == 0.1` (floor applied)\n\n**Given** a breakout where `current_price` is 15% above `high_52w`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` returns a signal  \n**Then** `signal.confidence == 1.0` (cap applied)\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py -k \"confidence\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC8 — Non-HOLD signal generated in realistic scenario\n\n**Given** a synthetic 400-candle daily dataset designed with:\n- A clear 6-month trend upward (SMA upward)\n- Normal volume for most bars, with a spike on the last bar\n- The last candle's close price slightly above the rolling 252-bar high\n\n**When** `generate_signal()` is called on the last candle  \n**Then** the return value is a `TradingSignal` with `decision == \"LONG\"`, proving the strategy is not permanently stuck in HOLD\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_generates_signal_in_realistic_scenario`\n\n---\n\n## AC9 — `should_reevaluate` always returns False\n\n**Given** any `ActivePosition` and `current_price`  \n**When** `strategy.should_reevaluate(position, current_price)` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `False`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_should_reevaluate_false`\n\n---\n\n## AC10 — Reference backtest completes without crash and PnL is calculated\n\n**Given** a test environment with database configured and AAPL daily data available for 2022–2023\n\n**When** the reference backtest from `QuantAgent-b8r-IM` is run:\n```python\nstrategy = FiftyTwoWeekHighStrategy()\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=datetime(2022, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2023, 12, 31),\n    assets=[\"AAPL\"],\n    timeframe=\"1d\",\n    initial_capital=100_000.0,\n    strategy=strategy,\n)\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"QuantAgent-b8r-reference\")\n```\n\n**Then**:\n- `backtest.run()` completes without raising any exception\n- `metrics.total_pnl` is a finite float (positive, negative, or zero)\n- `metrics.total_trades >= 0`\n- The run is logged with a name containing \"QuantAgent-b8r\"\n\n**Testable:** Manual integration test or `pytest tests/test_fifty_two_week_high_strategy.py::test_backtest_integration -m integration`\n\n---\n\n## Non-goals (explicitly excluded)\n\n- Performance targets (win rate, Sharpe ratio, drawdown)\n- Short-selling signals or short-side momentum\n- Proximity signal (without full breakout)\n- Multi-symbol parallel validation\n- Provider-specific behaviour or LLM integration\n- Comparison against RSI, Triple Screen, or LLMAgentStrategy\n","numLines":222,"startLine":1,"totalLines":222}}}
