{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FBkHFBWNxphu45Nj8WN2QF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Notes\n2\t\n3\tThis folder contains implementation notes, technical details, and post-implementation documentation for specific features and changes.\n4\t\n5\t## Reading Order\n6\t\n7\tAgents working in this repository should read implementation documents relevant to the feature being worked on:\n8\t\n9\t### Current Implementation Notes\n10\t- [backtest_data_pipeline_alignment.md](./backtest_data_pipeline_alignment.md) - OHLCV data pipeline alignment and remediation\n11\t- [20251130_Implementation_AgentParallelization.md](./20251130_Implementation_AgentParallelization.md) - Agent parallelization implementation details\n12\t- [SHORT_POSITIONS_IMPLEMENTATION.md](./SHORT_POSITIONS_IMPLEMENTATION.md) - Short position support implementation\n13\t- [IMPLEMENTATION_WEEK5_TRADING_EXECUTION.md](./IMPLEMENTATION_WEEK5_TRADING_EXECUTION.md) - Trading execution layer implementation\n14\t- [RISK_MANAGER_DUPLICATION.md](./RISK_MANAGER_DUPLICATION.md) - Risk manager duplication analysis and resolution\n15\t\n16\t## Current Truth\n17\t\n18\tImplementation notes document the actual code changes, technical decisions made during implementation, and any deviations from the original design. When working on related features:\n19\t\n20\t- Review relevant implementation notes to understand what was actually built\n21\t- Check for known issues or technical debt mentioned in the notes\n22\t- Use these documents to understand implementation patterns and conventions\n23\t\n24\t## Implementation Document Content\n25\t\n26\tImplementation documents should include:\n27\t\n28\t1. **Overview** - What was implemented\n29\t2. **Approach** - How it was implemented (key code changes)\n30\t3. **Deviations** - Any changes from the original design/plan\n31\t4. **Known Issues** - Technical debt or limitations\n32\t5. **Testing** - How the implementation was validated\n33\t\n34\t## Active Per-Change Implementation\n35\t\n36\t- [QuantAgent-c69-IM-llm-agent-strategy.md](./QuantAgent-c69-IM-llm-agent-strategy.md) - M1 Strategy 2: LLMAgentStrategy reference pipeline (m1, strategy)\n37\t- [QuantAgent-94d-IM-backtest-isolation.md](./QuantAgent-94d-IM-backtest-isolation.md) - Backtest Run ID Isolation (P1, bug)\n38\t\n39\t## Per-Change Implementation Documents\n40\t\n41\tPer-change implementation documents should follow this naming convention:\n42\t\n43\t```\n44\tQuantAgent-<issue-id>-IM-<short-slug>.md\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\tExample: `QuantAgent-a3f2dd-IM-fee-calculation.md`\n48\t\n49\tThese files describe implementation deltas and technical notes for specific changes linked to Beads issues (when applicable for system implementations).\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7c02214-d66b-4564-be8f-476a12f21292","uuid":"2639bbce-adb3-4e74-8911-5b831b16f2cb","timestamp":"2026-05-05T21:52:48.152Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/autodev-worktrees/techlead-20260505T213844Z/QuantAgent-b8r/implementer-20260505T213930Z/docs/06_implementation/README.md","content":"# Implementation Notes\n\nThis folder contains implementation notes, technical details, and post-implementation documentation for specific features and changes.\n\n## Reading Order\n\nAgents working in this repository should read implementation documents relevant to the feature being worked on:\n\n### Current Implementation Notes\n- [backtest_data_pipeline_alignment.md](./backtest_data_pipeline_alignment.md) - OHLCV data pipeline alignment and remediation\n- [20251130_Implementation_AgentParallelization.md](./20251130_Implementation_AgentParallelization.md) - Agent parallelization implementation details\n- [SHORT_POSITIONS_IMPLEMENTATION.md](./SHORT_POSITIONS_IMPLEMENTATION.md) - Short position support implementation\n- [IMPLEMENTATION_WEEK5_TRADING_EXECUTION.md](./IMPLEMENTATION_WEEK5_TRADING_EXECUTION.md) - Trading execution layer implementation\n- [RISK_MANAGER_DUPLICATION.md](./RISK_MANAGER_DUPLICATION.md) - Risk manager duplication analysis and resolution\n\n## Current Truth\n\nImplementation notes document the actual code changes, technical decisions made during implementation, and any deviations from the original design. When working on related features:\n\n- Review relevant implementation notes to understand what was actually built\n- Check for known issues or technical debt mentioned in the notes\n- Use these documents to understand implementation patterns and conventions\n\n## Implementation Document Content\n\nImplementation documents should include:\n\n1. **Overview** - What was implemented\n2. **Approach** - How it was implemented (key code changes)\n3. **Deviations** - Any changes from the original design/plan\n4. **Known Issues** - Technical debt or limitations\n5. **Testing** - How the implementation was validated\n\n## Active Per-Change Implementation\n\n- [QuantAgent-c69-IM-llm-agent-strategy.md](./QuantAgent-c69-IM-llm-agent-strategy.md) - M1 Strategy 2: LLMAgentStrategy reference pipeline (m1, strategy)\n- [QuantAgent-94d-IM-backtest-isolation.md](./QuantAgent-94d-IM-backtest-isolation.md) - Backtest Run ID Isolation (P1, bug)\n\n## Per-Change Implementation Documents\n\nPer-change implementation documents should follow this naming convention:\n\n```\nQuantAgent-<issue-id>-IM-<short-slug>.md\n```\n\nExample: `QuantAgent-a3f2dd-IM-fee-calculation.md`\n\nThese files describe implementation deltas and technical notes for specific changes linked to Beads issues (when applicable for system implementations).\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50}}}
